        "r": 276.266076,
        "b": 221.0862493388429
      },
      "content": "4.2.1.19 DATAPORT INTERFACE",
      "level": 4,
      "section_number": "4.2.1.19",
      "section_id": "sec_4_2_1_19",
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_263",
          "title": "FRONT PANEL KEYPAD MATRIX"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_4_2_1_19",
          "title": "4.2.1.19 DATAPORT INTERFACE"
        }
      ],
      "parent_section_id": "sec_auto_263",
      "section_level": 4,
      "page": 35,
      "chunk_hint": "section_heading",
      "semantic_role": "section_heading",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0249",
      "reading_order": 279,
      "section": "4.2.1.19 DATAPORT INTERFACE",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 107.99999999999997,
        "t": 206.10286681000002,
        "r": 540.0761898109995,
        "b": 137.20833468803278
      },
      "content": "The  CPU  communicates  with  an  external  computer  by  way  of  a  DataPort  interface. The DataPort interface provides for remote monitoring of up to 15 infusers using a host computer with a modified RS-232-D serial interface. Infusers are either connected directly to the host or in a daisy chain configuration using junction boxes that provide a 5 bit hard ID via DIP switches on the junction box. The DIP switches are buffered (peripheral PWA U8) and read by the CPU via the memory-mapped input/output (MMIO) port.",
      "section_id": "sec_4_2_1_19",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_auto_263",
      "section_level": 4,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_263",
          "title": "FRONT PANEL KEYPAD MATRIX"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_4_2_1_19",
          "title": "4.2.1.19 DATAPORT INTERFACE"
        }
      ],
      "page": 35,
      "chunk_hint": "section_start",
      "semantic_role": "overview",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0250",
      "reading_order": 280,
      "section": "4.2.1.19 DATAPORT INTERFACE",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 108.0,
        "t": 122.10402687390001,
        "r": 539.9398372741002,
        "b": 113.20859499193273
      },
      "content": "The DataPort system conforms to the EIA-232-D standard, with the following exceptions:",
      "section_id": "sec_4_2_1_19",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_auto_263",
      "section_level": 4,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_263",
          "title": "FRONT PANEL KEYPAD MATRIX"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_4_2_1_19",
          "title": "4.2.1.19 DATAPORT INTERFACE"
        }
      ],
      "page": 35,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0251",
      "reading_order": 281,
      "section": "4.2.1.19 DATAPORT INTERFACE",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 117.00006423619999,
        "t": 104.10419720179993,
        "r": 510.3935672092008,
        "b": 83.7487778138327
      },
      "content": "DataPort uses non-standard DB-15 and 6 pin modular connectors in addition to the standard DB-25 and DB-9 connectors",
      "section_id": "sec_4_2_1_19",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_auto_263",
      "section_level": 4,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_263",
          "title": "FRONT PANEL KEYPAD MATRIX"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_4_2_1_19",
          "title": "4.2.1.19 DATAPORT INTERFACE"
        }
      ],
      "page": 35,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0252",
      "reading_order": 282,
      "section": "4.2.1.19 DATAPORT INTERFACE",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 117.00026343639999,
        "t": 75.24417182589991,
        "r": 416.96130300179954,
        "b": 66.34873994393274
      },
      "content": "-With DataPort, more than one infuser is allowed on the line",
      "section_id": "sec_4_2_1_19",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_auto_263",
      "section_level": 4,
